00:20:50,207 --> 00:20:53,167
- Here we are. Great smoke spot.
- I got one for you.

474
00:20:53,168 --> 00:20:55,003
- Thanks.
- Okay. here we are.

475
00:20:57,965 --> 00:21:01,550
- Got something to ask the old guy?
- What I want to ask the old guy is…

476
00:21:01,551 --> 00:21:04,136
Well, so everyone's here
to find love, right?

477
00:21:04,137 --> 00:21:05,597
- Mmm.
- But…

478
00:21:06,223 --> 00:21:08,683
I'm going to tell you,
because it's just you and me right now,

479
00:21:08,684 --> 00:21:11,060
- but I've already failed at love twice.
- Oh. You have?

480
00:21:11,061 --> 00:21:14,105
Oh, but you know, I have a kid too.
So this is my kid's name, Rua.

481
00:21:14,106 --> 00:21:15,606
- Oh, is that so? Oh.
- Yeah.

482
00:21:15,607 --> 00:21:17,359
- So you're a single mom.
- That's right.

483
00:21:17,985 --> 00:21:19,986
- I am interested in someone.
- Hmm.

484
00:21:19,987 --> 00:21:23,406
But that person is already
head-over-heels for another girl.

485
00:21:23,407 --> 00:21:24,865
- Oh.
- I won't let that stop me, though.

486
00:21:24,866 --> 00:21:26,784
- Mmm, mmm.
- Once I'm in love, I mean.

487
00:21:26,785 --> 00:21:29,997
I'm just interested right now,
so I don't really know what to do.

488
00:21:30,580 --> 00:21:33,166
- Don't be afraid to fail.
- Right? That's true.

489
00:21:33,834 --> 00:21:36,627
- Even if you get rejected, go for it.
- Yeah, I'm perfectly okay with that.

490
00:21:36,628 --> 00:21:39,631
- We have that Okinawan positivity.
- Right? We don't let things get to us.

491
00:21:40,215 --> 00:21:43,759
In this world, there are so many you won't
get to meet during your lifetime.

492
00:21:43,760 --> 00:21:45,511
- I agree.
- So many you'll never meet.

493
00:21:45,512 --> 00:21:49,098
So, the fact that you were able
to meet is already fate, in a way.

494
00:21:49,099 --> 00:21:51,684
- At the very least, you'll be friends.
- Good point.

495
00:21:51,685 --> 00:21:53,686
It's that way with everything,
including love.

496
00:21:53,687 --> 00:21:56,772
Sometimes, people might suddenly
feel that rush and fall in love,

497
00:21:56,773 --> 00:21:58,733
but there are others who take their time.

498
00:21:58,734 --> 00:22:01,360
- That's true, yeah.
- Some people discover qualities they like.

499
00:22:01,361 --> 00:22:02,695
- Right? Right?
- Mmm-hmm.

500
00:22:02,696 --> 00:22:05,781
And then they develop feelings.
It all depends on the person.

501
00:22:05,782 --> 00:22:10,162
So there's no need to rush, but if you're
interested in him basically, well,

502
00:22:10,787 --> 00:22:12,788
he doesn't have to be your boyfriend.

503
00:22:12,789 --> 00:22:15,541
I think it's okay to start off just
as friends in the beginning, you know?

504
00:22:15,542 --> 00:22:17,919
- Mmm.
- It's not like making a brave attempt is…

505
00:22:18,670 --> 00:22:20,839
It isn't pathetic, not at all.
It's not pathetic.

506
00:22:21,423 --> 00:22:23,924
- Not taking a chance is more embarrassing.
- Yeah, that's right.

507
00:22:23,925 --> 00:22:24,760
You bet.

508
00:22:25,469 --> 00:22:27,471
- That's right. It's all good.
- Yeah.

509
00:22:28,013 --> 00:22:28,929
I got it.

510
00:22:28,930 --> 00:22:30,723
Do a good job raising
your little one, okay?

511
00:22:30,724 --> 00:22:31,974
- Yeah.
- All right then.

512
00:22:31,975 --> 00:22:35,519
I'll raise her with care. I have to find
someone who cherishes her like I do.

513
00:22:35,520 --> 00:22:38,939
Yes, you will. You will.
But if they fall in love with you,

514
00:22:38,940 --> 00:22:41,984
I'm sure they'll fall in love
with your kid automatically.

515
00:22:41,985 --> 00:22:44,488
So I don't think
you have to worry about that. I wouldn't.

516
00:22:45,280 --> 00:22:47,740
- Good luck.
- Yeah, I'll try my best. Thanks.

517
00:22:47,741 --> 00:22:49,825
- Thanks, Grandpa.
- Good luck.

518
00:22:49,826 --> 00:22:51,202
Thanks, Ma-chan.

519
00:22:51,203 --> 00:22:53,038
- It's done.
<i>- It's so cute.</i>

520
00:22:53,705 --> 00:22:56,415
- <i>It really is.</i>
- The yellow is so nice!

521
00:22:56,416 --> 00:23:00,461
- <i>It's super cute.</i>
- Well, thank you all for your hard work.

522
00:23:00,462 --> 00:23:03,131
Thank you so much.
Take care. We'll come again.

523
00:23:03,840 --> 00:23:05,424
- Thank you.
- Please come back.

524
00:23:05,425 --> 00:23:07,676
- We'll be back.
- I'll be waiting for you all.

525
00:23:07,677 --> 00:23:09,428
- Thank you.
- See you again.

526
00:23:09,429 --> 00:23:11,098
- Thanks, Ma-chan.
- Bye, take care.

527
00:23:12,307 --> 00:23:14,851
BADLY IN LOVE
MARINE ACADEMY

528
00:23:15,352 --> 00:23:17,436
- Seems like they're back.
- Here they are.

529
00:23:17,437 --> 00:23:18,437
Welcome back.

530
00:23:18,438 --> 00:23:21,190
- We finished the bench.
- Seriously? Where is it?

531
00:23:21,191 --> 00:23:23,568
We put your hopes
into this bench, Kamaken.

532
00:23:24,277 --> 00:23:26,071
- Welcome back.
- We're back.

533
00:23:26,905 --> 00:23:29,448
- Welcome back.
- What was that, huh?

534
00:23:29,449 --> 00:23:32,744
- <i>They're all buddies now.</i>
- <i>Yeah, even Tai-chan.</i>

535
00:23:34,287 --> 00:23:37,541
- It's in the classroom, let's go see it.
- Yeah, we want you all to come with us.

536
00:23:38,333 --> 00:23:40,418
- Shall we open the door?
- Shall!

537
00:23:40,419 --> 00:23:42,670
- I shall!
- Come in!

538
00:23:42,671 --> 00:23:44,755
- Whoa!
- Wow, amazing!

539
00:23:44,756 --> 00:23:46,507
- Wow, so cute!
- Isn't it amazing? Really good.

540
00:23:46,508 --> 00:23:48,217
- Amazing!
- It's adorable!

541
00:23:48,218 --> 00:23:50,261
- This makes me happy.
- Nice!

542
00:23:50,262 --> 00:23:52,555
- Like it?
- This is amazing!

543
00:23:52,556 --> 00:23:55,558
- Such a great job.
- We did it under the blazing sun.

544
00:23:55,559 --> 00:23:57,393
- You did good.
- Looks nice.

545
00:23:57,394 --> 00:23:59,645
- This is dope. So pretty.
- I like the pink.

546
00:23:59,646 --> 00:24:00,980
A gentle color.

547
00:24:00,981 --> 00:24:03,482
- Colors are good.
- They'll definitely be happy.

548
00:24:03,483 --> 00:24:04,734
The light blue is pretty.

549
00:24:05,652 --> 00:24:09,530
<i>Because you all worked hard
helping out the local community today,</i>

550
00:24:09,531 --> 00:24:11,490
<i>alcohol will be allowed at dinner.</i>

551
00:24:11,491 --> 00:24:14,076
- Hell yeah!
- Toss me to celebrate.

552
00:24:14,077 --> 00:24:15,578
Ready? And…

553
00:24:15,579 --> 00:24:18,164
Hurray! Hurray!

554
00:24:18,165 --> 00:24:21,584
<i>However, overdrinking is prohibited.</i>

555
00:24:21,585 --> 00:24:24,087
"Overdrinking is prohibited."

556
00:24:26,631 --> 00:24:27,507
Hey.

557
00:24:29,217 --> 00:24:30,343
Yo.

558
00:24:31,887 --> 00:24:33,929
- I'm so tired.
- Huh?

559
00:24:33,930 --> 00:24:36,433
- Aren't you tired?
- No, I'm not tired.

560
00:24:40,270 --> 00:24:41,437
So…

561
00:24:41,438 --> 00:24:44,232
Yeah, so, I wanted some time
with you today, because…

562
00:24:46,985 --> 00:24:48,944
- I want to say something.
- What is it?

563
00:24:48,945 --> 00:24:51,656
It's not something I want to say,
but something I have to tell you.

564
00:24:53,074 --> 00:24:55,577
And that's… I don't know, it's really…

565
00:24:56,995 --> 00:24:59,664
something I can only tell someone
who's special to me.

566
00:25:02,626 --> 00:25:03,668
Yeah.

567
00:25:05,170 --> 00:25:06,337
When I was 19 years old…

568
00:25:06,338 --> 00:25:07,379
Mmm-hmm.

569
00:25:07,380 --> 00:25:09,006
- I got married.
- Okay.

570
00:25:09,007 --> 00:25:10,509
- I'm 30 now, but…
- Mmm.

571
00:25:11,301 --> 00:25:14,346
I got married when I was 19 or 20,
and we had a kid together.

572
00:25:17,182 --> 00:25:18,850
And, well, we broke up, and…

573
00:25:20,227 --> 00:25:23,480
Well, I haven't seen them
in about four years now.

574
00:25:24,064 --> 00:25:25,565
- What?
- And that's because…

575
00:25:27,901 --> 00:25:28,985
Um…

576
00:25:30,529 --> 00:25:34,156
I was thinking about them,
or rather, I was thinking about my kid.

577
00:25:34,157 --> 00:25:35,867
- They have a new dad, you know?
- Mmm-hmm.

578
00:25:36,952 --> 00:25:38,787
I took that into consideration…

579
00:25:40,080 --> 00:25:42,249
and decided not to see
my kid anymore. Yeah.

580
00:25:44,751 --> 00:25:46,877
And that's what
I wanted to tell you today.

581
00:25:46,878 --> 00:25:47,712
Hmm.

582
00:25:49,923 --> 00:25:51,507
- Yeah.
- I think that's fine.

583
00:25:51,508 --> 00:25:53,300
- "I think that's fine"?
- I think it's fine.

584
00:25:53,301 --> 00:25:54,970
- It's fine?
- Well, I don't really…

585
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:58,556
- think anything of it.
- Hmm.

586
00:25:58,557 --> 00:26:00,516
If you want to see them,
you should see them.

587
00:26:00,517 --> 00:26:01,393
Mmm.

588
00:26:03,979 --> 00:26:05,980
I don't think there's
anything wrong about it.

589
00:26:05,981 --> 00:26:06,981
- Oh, really?
- Yeah.

590
00:26:06,982 --> 00:26:10,276
Is it something that burdens you?
Something like a weight?

591
00:26:10,277 --> 00:26:12,528
No, but I didn't
want to tell it to just anyone.

592
00:26:12,529 --> 00:26:14,029
- That's what you mean?
- Yeah.

593
00:26:14,030 --> 00:26:15,532
Okay, how do I put this?

594
00:26:17,284 --> 00:26:18,867
If hearing that made me leave,

595
00:26:18,868 --> 00:26:23,038
then I can't help but think
our relationship was never that strong.

596
00:26:23,039 --> 00:26:24,082
How do I put this…

597
00:26:25,417 --> 00:26:27,459
I don't want to be weak, either.

598
00:26:27,460 --> 00:26:28,377
Oh…

599
00:26:28,378 --> 00:26:31,171
Well, you did say you always
put up a brave front.

600
00:26:31,172 --> 00:26:34,426
- Like with… with a lot of things.
- I do.

601
00:26:35,010 --> 00:26:37,261
- Mmm.
- I guess I don't show my weaknesses.

602
00:26:37,262 --> 00:26:39,221
Ah, you don't like to show them?

603
00:26:39,222 --> 00:26:40,807
Well, mm…

604
00:26:42,434 --> 00:26:45,811
With my first relationship,
I would cry in secret and stuff.

605
00:26:45,812 --> 00:26:46,771
Oh…

606
00:26:49,232 --> 00:26:51,692
- Your first?
- Yeah, because he was physically abusive.

607
00:26:51,693 --> 00:26:54,153
- Oh.
- So I cried in secret and stuff.

608
00:26:54,154 --> 00:26:55,280
Oh, you did?

609
00:26:56,406 --> 00:27:00,034
But I seriously can't imagine how a guy
could abuse his partner in any way.

610
00:27:00,035 --> 00:27:02,369
Mmm, there was
a lot of stuff that happened.

611
00:27:02,370 --> 00:27:04,706
Like, he strangled me and pushed me over.

612
00:27:06,583 --> 00:27:07,625
That kind of stuff…

613
00:27:07,626 --> 00:27:09,210
- Oh…
- Yeah.

614
00:27:12,714 --> 00:27:14,924
But, you know, I'm happy that you told me.

615
00:27:16,760 --> 00:27:18,594
What?

616
00:27:18,595 --> 00:27:19,887
Huh? No, it's nothing.

617
00:27:19,888 --> 00:27:21,305
<i>Her smile is so cute.</i>

618
00:27:21,306 --> 00:27:23,308
<i>She's letting out a smile. It's so cute.</i>

619
00:27:25,352 --> 00:27:26,895
Well, I was surprised.

620
00:27:27,479 --> 00:27:29,022
It turns out that Kamaken…

621
00:27:29,814 --> 00:27:32,776
had more weighing on his mind
than I thought he did.

622
00:27:33,318 --> 00:27:35,195
Like, with my dad currently…

623
00:27:36,279 --> 00:27:37,822
back in high school,

624
00:27:38,823 --> 00:27:42,369
that's when he and I actually,
we stopped seeing each other.

625
00:27:44,454 --> 00:27:45,413
So, like…

626
00:27:47,666 --> 00:27:51,711
because, well, I'm experiencing it
as the child in the situation,

627
00:27:52,545 --> 00:27:55,840
I feel like
not being able to see each other

628
00:27:56,716 --> 00:27:57,966
is…

629
00:27:57,967 --> 00:28:00,804
really painful. Yeah, that's what I think.

630
00:28:02,305 --> 00:28:04,224
- That was nice.
- Yeah.

631
00:28:04,849 --> 00:28:07,352
So this means that
Rinrin and Kamaken are solid.

632
00:28:07,852 --> 00:28:10,521
- But, didn't he say something to Mimi too?
- He certainly did.

633
00:28:10,522 --> 00:28:11,856
- Ah!
- Kamaken, I mean.

634
00:28:12,524 --> 00:28:13,774
Wait, that's right.

635
00:28:13,775 --> 00:28:16,026
"Everyone was going for you,
so I gave up."

636
00:28:16,027 --> 00:28:19,488
- Like he withdrew.
- That was a little concerning, right?

637
00:28:19,489 --> 00:28:21,533
It's like, "Don't say that!" You know?

638
00:28:22,325 --> 00:28:25,411
- She was waiting for you.
- You were waiting for me?

639
00:28:25,412 --> 00:28:26,787
- So cute.
- Enough.

640
00:28:26,788 --> 00:28:28,622
- I'll get some.
- Defrost that.

641
00:28:28,623 --> 00:28:30,165
Leave it out of Rinrin's.

642
00:28:30,166 --> 00:28:31,959
So we'll wrap them
in gyoza wrappers, right?

643
00:28:31,960 --> 00:28:34,294
- Yeah, we're doing a whole bunch.
- Go cook with Mimi.

644
00:28:34,295 --> 00:28:36,380
There's a lot of stuff
I'll need your help with later on.

645
00:28:36,381 --> 00:28:38,632
- Here.
- Hey. You wanna smoke?

646
00:28:38,633 --> 00:28:39,467
Yeah, sure.

647
00:28:40,093 --> 00:28:42,261
I've also been
to Chidori Park in Kanagawa.

648
00:28:42,262 --> 00:28:45,681
Chidori Park?
Isn't that near Minato Mirai?

649
00:28:45,682 --> 00:28:47,433
This'll take 15 minutes, don't open it.

650
00:28:47,434 --> 00:28:48,768
You can really taste it.

651
00:28:57,902 --> 00:29:00,447
- Fifteen-minute break.
- Use it if you want.

652
00:29:01,740 --> 00:29:04,825
You know, I've been thinking
about it ever since I came here…

653
00:29:04,826 --> 00:29:05,784
Hmm.

654
00:29:05,785 --> 00:29:08,454
…and I think I'm probably
not the type of guy

655
00:29:08,455 --> 00:29:11,039
who wants to go out
and try to win someone's heart.

656
00:29:11,040 --> 00:29:12,249
I see.

657
00:29:12,250 --> 00:29:15,335
- I think, "This is too much trouble."
- I get that, man.

658
00:29:15,336 --> 00:29:18,797
I mean, it's like, whatever.
I'm just not sure it's worth all of this.

659
00:29:18,798 --> 00:29:21,634
- Oh, really?
- Yeah, I mean, honestly, Kamaken…

660
00:29:22,218 --> 00:29:24,845
I found myself not really caring
about pursuing it anymore.

661
00:29:24,846 --> 00:29:25,889
- Are you serious?
- For real.

662
00:29:26,598 --> 00:29:27,806
No way.

663
00:29:27,807 --> 00:29:29,850
- Isn't the situation changing?
- I'm being serious.

664
00:29:29,851 --> 00:29:30,894
- Really?
- Yeah, and…

665
00:29:31,686 --> 00:29:34,230
- I found myself thinking that.
- Have you talked to Mimi today?

666
00:29:35,398 --> 00:29:37,983
Like at any point?
Because I haven't seen you two talking.

667
00:29:37,984 --> 00:29:40,903
Well, you know, we haven't
really talked about anything--

668
00:29:40,904 --> 00:29:42,738
- Let's do the thing.
- Oh, yes.

669
00:29:42,739 --> 00:29:44,323
- Ayacheru, can you finish this?
- Sure.

670
00:29:44,324 --> 00:29:45,825
- Sorry. Thank you.
- Okay.

671
00:29:48,703 --> 00:29:51,288
<i>What? What's wrong?</i>

672
00:29:51,289 --> 00:29:54,125
<i>So it was a big deal
that she went to Tai-chan.</i>

673
00:29:55,210 --> 00:29:56,126
It's normal.

674
00:29:56,127 --> 00:29:58,587
- Why are you so loud today?
- Let's eat!

675
00:29:58,588 --> 00:30:00,547
Cheers!

676
00:30:00,548 --> 00:30:03,342
- Thank you. Let's eat.
- Cheers!

677
00:30:03,343 --> 00:30:05,260
- Welcome back.
- Cheers!

678
00:30:05,261 --> 00:30:07,846
- Good job.
- Let's get it going!

679
00:30:07,847 --> 00:30:09,306
- Cheers.
- Sara, good job.

680
00:30:09,307 --> 00:30:12,017
- Wow, this is yummy.
- Lots of alcohol.

681
00:30:12,018 --> 00:30:15,187
- You haven't eaten anything.
- I'm drinking a lot. Seriously.

682
00:30:15,188 --> 00:30:17,773
Doesn't that make it harder?
To eat I mean?

683
00:30:17,774 --> 00:30:19,691
- Taste so good.
- I don't know.

684
00:30:19,692 --> 00:30:21,778
Hmm, tastes like it.
I don't want this one.

685
00:30:22,320 --> 00:30:25,323
SMOKERS' LOUNGE

686
00:30:26,115 --> 00:30:27,908
Wow, Kazuma, you're in a harem.

687
00:30:27,909 --> 00:30:30,410
Surrounded by two beautiful women
with tattoos.

688
00:30:30,411 --> 00:30:31,787
This is a good time.

689
00:30:31,788 --> 00:30:33,497
It is. We have to cherish it.

690
00:30:33,498 --> 00:30:35,375
It's a precious, irreplaceable time.

691
00:30:35,875 --> 00:30:38,670
I would also like to take a tour
of the guys' room.

692
00:30:39,796 --> 00:30:40,922
- You wanna come?
- You should go.

693
00:30:43,132 --> 00:30:44,883
- The guys' room?
- Yeah.

694
00:30:44,884 --> 00:30:46,761
Isn't the girls' room super fancy?

695
00:30:47,303 --> 00:30:50,055
- It is big.
- Yeah, the girls' room is so big.

696
00:30:50,056 --> 00:30:52,266
Wow, nice. Hello.

697
00:30:52,267 --> 00:30:54,184
- Hey…
- Come in, come in.

698
00:30:54,185 --> 00:30:55,894
- Don't be shy.
- This room has a manly vibe.

699
00:30:55,895 --> 00:30:57,813
Smells better than the girls' room.

700
00:30:57,814 --> 00:31:01,693
Oh, and everyone said that you're good
at drawing. I wanna see it too.

701
00:31:04,529 --> 00:31:07,781
This one is a traditional style,
Japanese traditional tattoo.

702
00:31:07,782 --> 00:31:10,577
- These are like study pieces.
- Mm-hmm. This is cool.

703
00:31:11,744 --> 00:31:13,288
Wow. What is this <i>bonji?</i>

704
00:31:14,372 --> 00:31:17,292
- This is my Chinese zodiac sign.
- Oh, in which year were you born?

705
00:31:17,792 --> 00:31:20,252
- The year of the rabbit.
- Oh, rabbit. Cute.

706
00:31:20,253 --> 00:31:22,713
I was going to draw
Sara's Chinese zodiac sign too.

707
00:31:22,714 --> 00:31:24,798
- Which year?
- Hers is the same as mine.

708
00:31:24,799 --> 00:31:27,010
- Rabbit? You two are the same age?
- Rabbit. Yeah, exactly.

709
00:31:27,594 --> 00:31:28,428
Wow.

710
00:31:29,012 --> 00:31:32,055
This is really nice. I've thought about
becoming a tattoo artist too.

711
00:31:32,056 --> 00:31:34,434
- You did say you wanted to try being one.
- Yeah, I did.

712
00:31:35,018 --> 00:31:36,185
These are amazing.

713
00:31:37,437 --> 00:31:38,563
They're so nice.

714
00:31:40,940 --> 00:31:44,359
Do you draw here
when you have free time? Making a new one?

715
00:31:44,360 --> 00:31:46,236
Yeah. I'm working on the drawing

716
00:31:46,237 --> 00:31:47,614
- I'm going to give Sara.
- I see.

717
00:31:54,871 --> 00:31:55,914
Should we talk?

718
00:31:57,916 --> 00:31:59,750
- Yeah 'cause earlier…
- Yeah.

719
00:31:59,751 --> 00:32:02,127
I was spending time with you today,

720
00:32:02,128 --> 00:32:05,255
and you said that you wanted
to talk to me, so I thought--

721
00:32:05,256 --> 00:32:06,214
Yeah, let's talk.

722
00:32:06,215 --> 00:32:07,466
- Yeah.
- So, um--

723
00:32:07,467 --> 00:32:11,511
It kind of makes me think,
because you have a thing with Rinrin.

724
00:32:11,512 --> 00:32:12,596
Yeah.

725
00:32:12,597 --> 00:32:16,183
We don't have many days left,
and there are people thinking about me.

726
00:32:16,184 --> 00:32:18,060
- Yeah.
- And they're telling me their feelings.

727
00:32:18,061 --> 00:32:20,771
I wouldn't want to reach the end
without talking to you, too.

728
00:32:20,772 --> 00:32:24,192
Especially since, well I was thinking
about this while working today…

729
00:32:24,734 --> 00:32:27,236
- And, well, you know I thought that…
- Yeah.

730
00:32:28,196 --> 00:32:30,949
Because of our age,
I felt like you'd understand me.

731
00:32:31,532 --> 00:32:32,575
That's a good point.

732
00:32:33,868 --> 00:32:36,537
You know, back when
I was going to fight Kazuma,

733
00:32:37,455 --> 00:32:39,666
and you were the one to stop that fight…

734
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:43,211
I don't know, I've been interested in you.

735
00:32:43,920 --> 00:32:46,880
I'm 29 years old,
and I've experienced a lot in this life.

736
00:32:46,881 --> 00:32:47,798
Hmm.

737
00:32:47,799 --> 00:32:51,259
Considering all of that,
I honestly thought at the time,

738
00:32:51,260 --> 00:32:52,844
"You know, I really like Kamaken."

739
00:32:52,845 --> 00:32:54,846
Wait, really?

740
00:32:54,847 --> 00:32:56,099
- That's what I thought.
- When?

741
00:33:01,270 --> 00:33:03,355
Wow, I didn't expect this.

742
00:33:03,356 --> 00:33:05,148
But you must have had some kind of idea.

743
00:33:05,149 --> 00:33:08,360
Because when we were hanging out
and smoking behind the gym,

744
00:33:08,361 --> 00:33:09,779
you told me how you felt.

745
00:33:10,738 --> 00:33:11,780
Well, that's true.

746
00:33:11,781 --> 00:33:14,826
I thought, "Why do I have to lose
to a 20-year-old?"

747
00:33:17,495 --> 00:33:21,541
I had absolutely no idea.
You're being pursued by three guys. Right?

748
00:33:22,333 --> 00:33:23,584
And, you know,

749
00:33:24,585 --> 00:33:27,505
Maru, Tai-chan, and Rune,
they are all pursuing you.

750
00:33:28,047 --> 00:33:32,343
And I said I would back off.
I told everyone I would, and I did.

751
00:33:33,886 --> 00:33:36,514
- Yeah.
- Don't back off. This is <i>Badly In Love.</i>

752
00:33:39,058 --> 00:33:41,310
I came here to see
what you're made of, seriously.

753
00:33:41,853 --> 00:33:42,854
You have a point.

754
00:33:43,688 --> 00:33:46,356
I'm sorry, but I want to be clear.

755
00:33:46,357 --> 00:33:47,817
There are three guys pursuing you.

756
00:33:48,526 --> 00:33:51,821
Do you think you've narrowed it down
to one person yet?

757
00:33:52,405 --> 00:33:53,406
I haven't decided yet.

758
00:33:54,615 --> 00:33:55,658
Oh, I see.

759
00:33:58,661 --> 00:34:00,746
- You really haven't?
- There's something missing,

760
00:34:00,747 --> 00:34:01,873
in each of them.

761
00:34:05,752 --> 00:34:09,171
- I'm going to get a drink. Excuse me.
- You're going back?

762
00:34:09,172 --> 00:34:10,547
I don't know, I mean…

763
00:34:10,548 --> 00:34:12,508
Well, there are a lot of guys
who want to talk to you.

764
00:34:13,426 --> 00:34:15,595
Oh, so I have your permission?

765
00:34:16,846 --> 00:34:19,806
- No, wait. That's not what I meant.
- Can I go? I'm asking you.

766
00:34:19,807 --> 00:34:21,392
So tell me, is it okay if I go?

767
00:34:24,896 --> 00:34:25,813
Kamaken.

768
00:34:31,194 --> 00:34:32,736
I'm a little scared now.

769
00:34:32,737 --> 00:34:34,447
- This girl's too strong.
- I can go, right?

770
00:34:36,824 --> 00:34:39,077
Oh, what should I do?

771
00:34:46,876 --> 00:34:48,961
This is hard. What do I do?

772
00:34:49,545 --> 00:34:51,546
- What?
- Kamaken!

773
00:34:51,547 --> 00:34:52,423
What's going on?

774
00:34:53,716 --> 00:34:55,300
What is this?

775
00:34:55,301 --> 00:34:57,178
Oh, this is so hard.

776
00:35:00,264 --> 00:35:02,682
I don't know what to do?
Ryopi, can I talk to you for a second?

777
00:35:02,683 --> 00:35:03,810
Oh, sure, no problem.

778
00:35:05,019 --> 00:35:07,312
I'm really at a crossroads
right now, seriously.

779
00:35:07,313 --> 00:35:08,189
I can imagine.

780
00:35:09,690 --> 00:35:13,110
- In the end, I think it's all up to you.
- I wasn't thinking about it at all today.

781
00:35:13,111 --> 00:35:15,445
- Oh.
- I wasn't thinking about talking to Mimi.

782
00:35:15,446 --> 00:35:18,615
I was just being myself and trying
to have fun. That's how I behaved.

783
00:35:18,616 --> 00:35:21,118
I think that was good.
I think she got that.

784
00:35:21,119 --> 00:35:24,079
That's why Mimi wanted
to talk to you today, right?

785
00:35:24,080 --> 00:35:26,332
I mean, she's probably thinking
about you too.

786
00:35:30,711 --> 00:35:33,046
- Seriously, I just don't know what to do.
- I feel you.

787
00:35:33,047 --> 00:35:35,007
I am at a major crossroads right now.

788
00:35:37,343 --> 00:35:39,511
<i>But, you know,
Rinrin is the kind of girl that--</i>

789
00:35:39,512 --> 00:35:41,681
<i>It's going to be terrible
if she finds out.</i>

790
00:35:45,434 --> 00:35:49,020
I mean, there are six guys
at the school with me right now.

791
00:35:49,021 --> 00:35:53,775
But to be honest, there's actually no one
I want to pursue for myself.

792
00:35:53,776 --> 00:35:56,820
And really, I think
it's because of my trauma.

793
00:35:56,821 --> 00:35:58,488
That's what I'd have to say.

794
00:35:58,489 --> 00:36:01,325
I just honestly have
a hard time trusting men.

795
00:36:02,618 --> 00:36:03,452
Um…

796
00:36:05,872 --> 00:36:09,207
It all started
the first time I'd ever been cheated on.

797
00:36:09,208 --> 00:36:10,376
I was a student.

798
00:36:11,711 --> 00:36:12,545
And, well…

799
00:36:14,088 --> 00:36:15,464
Yeah, at that time…

800
00:36:17,049 --> 00:36:18,258
Um…

801
00:36:18,259 --> 00:36:19,886
Well, you see, I was…

802
00:36:20,845 --> 00:36:22,262
pregnant with his child.

803
00:36:22,263 --> 00:36:25,349
But I remember thinking
I was still just a student.

804
00:36:25,975 --> 00:36:28,227
We were still kids,
and we were going to have a kid.

805
00:36:29,187 --> 00:36:32,523
We couldn't imagine that,
so we talked it over.

806
00:36:33,399 --> 00:36:36,776
And, in the end, we made the decision
to give up the baby, but,

807
00:36:36,777 --> 00:36:39,405
he cheated on me during that time,
which made me…

808
00:36:40,656 --> 00:36:41,490
well…

809
00:36:42,491 --> 00:36:46,077
So, from that point on,
more than other girls,

810
00:36:46,078 --> 00:36:47,872
I started to think of men as…

811
00:36:49,332 --> 00:36:50,415
You know…

812
00:36:50,416 --> 00:36:54,544
I was checking each man thoroughly to see
if he was the one who wouldn't cheat,

813
00:36:54,545 --> 00:36:56,005
lie, or go to other girls.

814
00:36:59,592 --> 00:37:01,010
I came here to find love,

815
00:37:01,844 --> 00:37:03,262
but I'm not very good at it.

816
00:37:10,561 --> 00:37:12,146
And recently, it felt like…

817
00:37:15,149 --> 00:37:19,904
Yeah, it's something I really worry about
so much, I can't sleep. It's on my mind.

818
00:37:20,655 --> 00:37:22,823
I worry about it, even at work.

819
00:37:24,367 --> 00:37:25,534
Yeah, so…

820
00:37:27,203 --> 00:37:28,537
That's it. Hmm.

821
00:37:29,538 --> 00:37:30,706
I can't figure it out.

822
00:37:34,543 --> 00:37:37,337
It's like she's dealing with
the men as if she's at work.

823
00:37:37,338 --> 00:37:39,839
- I think so.
- That's what I'm getting from this.

824
00:37:39,840 --> 00:37:40,675
Also,

825
00:37:41,467 --> 00:37:44,386
I'm sensing she
might not know how to love.

826
00:37:44,387 --> 00:37:46,554
- How she behaves with Kamaken you mean?
- Yeah.

827
00:37:46,555 --> 00:37:48,307
- When she asked, "Can I go?"
- Yeah.

828
00:37:48,933 --> 00:37:52,060
Judging from that behavior,
I think she's struggling with herself.

829
00:37:52,061 --> 00:37:53,645
- Mmm.
- That's what I think.

830
00:37:53,646 --> 00:37:56,731
She was obviously hurt
very deeply in her life.

831
00:37:56,732 --> 00:37:58,942
- So, you can tell she's serious.
- I know.

832
00:37:58,943 --> 00:38:02,946
You know, she didn't come
to <i>Badly In Love</i> just to mess around.

833
00:38:02,947 --> 00:38:04,615
- She was the hardest to read.
- Yeah.

834
00:38:06,534 --> 00:38:07,660
- Let's talk.
- Yeah.

835
00:38:09,203 --> 00:38:11,080
- <i>Wait, what is he doing?</i>
- <i>Oh!</i>

836
00:38:11,872 --> 00:38:13,081
<i>Scary.</i>

837
00:38:13,082 --> 00:38:15,668
Okay, so…

838
00:38:18,713 --> 00:38:21,090
I don't know if Mimi was drunk or not,

839
00:38:22,508 --> 00:38:24,927
but she told me, like,
"Come after me more."

840
00:38:26,220 --> 00:38:28,514
Like, "Are you fine
with how it is right now?"

841
00:38:29,265 --> 00:38:31,058
- That's what she said.
- Mmm… And?

842
00:38:33,311 --> 00:38:37,022
But I wanted to bring you here
to tell you what we talked about.

843
00:38:37,023 --> 00:38:39,859
And… Yeah. Mmm.

844
00:38:41,694 --> 00:38:44,988
And It's true that I did want
to talk to her a little more.

845
00:38:44,989 --> 00:38:46,281
Mmm-hmm.

846
00:38:46,282 --> 00:38:47,116
But…

847
00:38:48,075 --> 00:38:51,078
you were the one who made
those feelings go away.

848
00:38:53,873 --> 00:38:54,999
But, I…

849
00:38:57,376 --> 00:38:59,419
I didn't know she had that feeling.

850
00:38:59,420 --> 00:39:03,506
Mimi wanted me to--
She was actually interested in me.

851
00:39:03,507 --> 00:39:05,968
I thought she had no interest
in me. Really.

852
00:39:07,345 --> 00:39:10,597
So, I don't know if that's really
how she is feeling or not.

853
00:39:10,598 --> 00:39:13,142
Hmm. Then you should talk about it.

854
00:39:15,102 --> 00:39:16,062
Hmm.

855
00:39:18,481 --> 00:39:21,567
It's up to you.
I don't really care what you decide.

856
00:39:28,783 --> 00:39:30,159
- I get that.
- Yeah.

857
00:39:34,330 --> 00:39:35,413
It's up to you.

858
00:39:35,414 --> 00:39:36,582
- Up to me?
- Yeah.

859
00:39:40,961 --> 00:39:44,298
Anyway, until you make up your mind,
don't do anything to me, okay?

860
00:39:46,759 --> 00:39:48,135
- I shouldn't.
- Yeah.

861
00:39:48,928 --> 00:39:51,429
<i>That's so cool! You're so cool, Rinrin!</i>

862
00:39:51,430 --> 00:39:53,516
<i>She's so cool.</i>

863
00:40:00,481 --> 00:40:01,565
Are we done here?

864
00:40:17,873 --> 00:40:20,500
Well, it would've been better
if I could've just said,

865
00:40:20,501 --> 00:40:23,002
"No, I'm into Rinrin," when she said that.

866
00:40:23,003 --> 00:40:24,130
But I couldn't say it.

867
00:40:25,131 --> 00:40:26,173
How do I put it?

868
00:40:28,175 --> 00:40:30,010
My heart is in so much turmoil.

869
00:40:31,137 --> 00:40:32,972
I just don't know what I should do.

870
00:40:44,733 --> 00:40:46,026
Good morning.

871
00:40:49,655 --> 00:40:52,407
Yeah, well,
let's put aside the romance stuff.

872
00:40:52,408 --> 00:40:54,368
- Mmm-hmm.
- But I'm rooting for you.

873
00:40:55,911 --> 00:40:57,830
<i>She has such a big heart.</i>

874
00:40:59,957 --> 00:41:00,791
Mmm.

875
00:41:02,835 --> 00:41:03,669
Mmm.

876
00:41:04,712 --> 00:41:05,546
Good luck.

877
00:41:06,755 --> 00:41:08,840
- I'm rooting for you from afar.
- From afar?

878
00:41:08,841 --> 00:41:12,094
<i>- She's so cool.</i>
- You don't have to do it from the shadows.

879
00:41:14,221 --> 00:41:18,641
To tell you straight, I was actually
thinking of confessing my love to you.

880
00:41:18,642 --> 00:41:19,477
Mmm.

881
00:41:21,896 --> 00:41:24,523
Well, I know you've been
saying that from the start.

882
00:41:25,149 --> 00:41:28,110
And it's true that I was happy
about that when I heard it.

883
00:41:28,736 --> 00:41:29,944
Mmm-hmm.

884
00:41:29,945 --> 00:41:32,989
- I'm very thankful to you.
- <i>Her eyes have changed.</i>

885
00:41:32,990 --> 00:41:34,365
- <i>Yeah.</i>
- <i>Right.</i>

886
00:41:34,366 --> 00:41:35,783
Yes.

887
00:41:35,784 --> 00:41:37,035
- What is it?
- Nothing.

888
00:41:37,036 --> 00:41:39,205
I'm not doing anything.

889
00:41:40,289 --> 00:41:41,831
- I'm so grateful.
- For what?

890
00:41:41,832 --> 00:41:44,752
- I'm grateful that you're here.
- Oh, are you? I see.

891
00:41:52,468 --> 00:41:57,681
So, yesterday, you talked to Kamaken,
and you said you were interested in him.

892
00:42:00,100 --> 00:42:02,978
I feel like the number of people
is increasing day by day.

893
00:42:06,732 --> 00:42:09,693
- Mmm.
- You haven't smiled at me once.

894
00:42:10,444 --> 00:42:12,321
Not since we were cooking yesterday.

895
00:42:17,409 --> 00:42:20,745
I want to come at you straight
and be completely honest with you.

896
00:42:20,746 --> 00:42:22,957
I want us both
to face each other honestly.

897
00:42:24,041 --> 00:42:25,751
But I need you to face me too.

898
00:42:27,253 --> 00:42:31,215
Otherwise, you know, I honestly wonder
if it's worth me trying to face you.

899
00:42:35,261 --> 00:42:36,971
Because I'm thinking seriously.

900
00:42:40,224 --> 00:42:41,475
- I understand.
- Yeah.

901
00:42:45,104 --> 00:42:47,106
- You're so right.
- Mmm-hmm.

902
00:42:48,816 --> 00:42:49,858
Mmm-hmm.

903
00:42:53,821 --> 00:42:56,281
- I wonder. He likes her so much…
- Yeah.

904
00:42:56,282 --> 00:42:59,450
- Why doesn't he act a little more excited?
- I know.

905
00:42:59,451 --> 00:43:01,369
- Rune is a little stiff and intimidating.
- Yeah.

906
00:43:01,370 --> 00:43:04,289
No, it's more like,
he comes across as a little critical.

907
00:43:04,290 --> 00:43:06,541
- It might be working against him.
- Hmm.

908
00:43:06,542 --> 00:43:10,253
And Ayacheru,
she's still set on Maru, right?

909
00:43:10,254 --> 00:43:11,963
She's like, "I'm rooting for you."

910
00:43:11,964 --> 00:43:14,758
But what do you think
about how she feels, sensei?

911
00:43:15,884 --> 00:43:19,053
I think that by acting all big-hearted,

912
00:43:19,054 --> 00:43:21,639
she's trying to secure
a fallback place for Maru.

913
00:43:21,640 --> 00:43:22,599
Mmm.

914
00:43:22,600 --> 00:43:24,392
- So he can come back.
- Oh.

915
00:43:24,393 --> 00:43:28,021
And she's trying to make sure he knows
that place will always be there for him.

916
00:43:28,022 --> 00:43:29,897
- Mmm.
- That's what she's saying, right?

917
00:43:29,898 --> 00:43:30,982
Hmm.

918
00:43:30,983 --> 00:43:33,943
- She still likes him, right?
- I think she still likes him.

919
00:43:33,944 --> 00:43:34,903
Hmm.

920
00:43:36,155 --> 00:43:40,199
<i>The graduation ceremony
is finally the day after tomorrow.</i>

921
00:43:40,200 --> 00:43:44,245
<i>And tomorrow,
is the appreciation party for the locals.</i>

922
00:43:44,246 --> 00:43:46,080
MARU - AYACHERU

923
00:43:46,081 --> 00:43:47,874
<i>Let's start the final preparation.</i>

924
00:43:47,875 --> 00:43:49,043
I fell asleep.

925
00:43:49,752 --> 00:43:52,670
- I like that.
- This is nice. Really nice.

926
00:43:52,671 --> 00:43:55,089
- Yeah, it's starting to look good.
- I'm hot.

927
00:43:55,090 --> 00:43:56,675
- Hey, that's nice.
- "It's free!"

928
00:43:57,343 --> 00:43:58,509
Is it done?

929
00:43:58,510 --> 00:44:01,262
- "It's free!"
- "It's free" is a nice touch.

930
00:44:01,263 --> 00:44:03,264
It's like, "Welcome in!"

931
00:44:03,265 --> 00:44:05,558
Isn't there an extra line
in the "free" character?

932
00:44:05,559 --> 00:44:06,726
I made a mistake.

933
00:44:06,727 --> 00:44:08,353
MASSAGE BOOTH
FREE!

934
00:44:08,354 --> 00:44:10,813
- It's a prank.
- There are five lines. A prank?

935
00:44:10,814 --> 00:44:13,025
FOOD

936
00:44:17,237 --> 00:44:19,030
- Kahochi has a fever.
- She does?

937
00:44:19,031 --> 00:44:21,407
- She does, it's pretty bad.
- Kaho, take care.

938
00:44:21,408 --> 00:44:22,742
Aw.

939
00:44:22,743 --> 00:44:25,370
- Wait, you have a fever?
- I do. It's 37.8.

940
00:44:25,371 --> 00:44:27,205
- Oh, no.
- That's bad.

941
00:44:27,206 --> 00:44:28,790
Poor Kahochi.

942
